gned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-7)^{2}}=\\sqrt{114}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5924037a-ddc3-5f50-b4b0-1bd813cef255"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection/756768d78cd65dc7baee3f82fc0925760f130ea052feeacb91e0b166dbd8fc90" :answer/id #uuid "b0826008-218c-5bd6-9a6e-6de0b4c48bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{110}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection/33a3f214ac39c1120abfe6bc86b7e4cdeeecfe239fa5c065011274e009276610" :answer/id #uuid "6c9dcec6-947a-53af-8864-b9ad24b5f651" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection/8ecf42d61d85deb9b7e1281c4e31fb1576dec9e17aa5c6cf3d61e8c06707283b" :answer/id #uuid "c1cb192f-b86d-5b23-9322-ec6f0c46a444" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{111}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection/aad2f73b3d98c2c84885833ca81999af73544acae72b64f9df8052ce456f5e03" :answer/id #uuid "8c94b5d8-367e-578c-8769-b4fd4cf13df4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{101}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935" :answer/id #uuid "424a3d58-03b4-5418-a7c1-c0351c5c2656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "769a5227-f164-5a89-952a-4843116574bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85284/selection/756768d78cd65dc7baee3f82fc0925760f130ea052feeacb91e0b166dbd8fc90" :answer-field/choices ["q-85284/selection/756768d78cd65dc7baee3f82fc0925760f130ea052feeacb91e0b166dbd8fc90" "q-85284/selection/33a3f214ac39c1120abfe6bc86b7e4cdeeecfe239fa5c065011274e009276610" "q-85284/selection/8ecf42d61d85deb9b7e1281c4e31fb1576dec9e17aa5c6cf3d61e8c06707283b" "q-85284/selection/aad2f73b3d98c2c84885833ca81999af73544acae72b64f9df8052ce456f5e03" "q-85284/selection/4ef0fcc340e40ad6bcef1c832215cd28abf240aabeed43296dfece28d20d1935"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85284" :question/id #uuid "3d64d189-36ec-5faa-a1eb-5573a00d3bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-85284" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{110}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-85284/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5924037a-ddc3-5f50-b4b0-1bd813cef255"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85909/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "5410eac1-24d4-5bc8-a29c-9a371267e1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85909/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "e8a2eb2b-077c-574b-9d49-e28b74d5b70c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85909/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #u